  "live_records": {
    "q-316898": {
      "dom_id": "step-q316898",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251078/assets/6a67039e1192670e638fbaf88814a6474c9262dee32117d4cdb48db0f0d904fb.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $a$ is perpendicular to $b$, $|a|=12$ and $|b|=9.$ Find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a right triangle. So, we can use Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={12}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =144+81 \\\\  & =225\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{225}=15.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
